1
00:00:00,840 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,577
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:35,240
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:52,577
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:55,277
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:58,477
Raise the sails and take the helm.

18
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place.

19
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,877
That the end of the map reveals.

20
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:06,717
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:10,117
Till someone proves it real.

22
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,437
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times.

23
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,257
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:24,300
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:28,217
So come aboard and bring along.

27
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,540
All your hopes and dreams.

28
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,857
Together we will find everything.

29
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,000
That we're looking for.

30
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,677
There's always room for you.

31
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,440
If you wanna be my friend.

32
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,780
We are, we are on a cruise.

33
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,720
We are?

34
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:54,900
He destroyed the fin!

35
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,480
He's trying to sink my ship.

36
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,940
You dare defy me?

37
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,560
Dean, blow his head off right now!

38
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,040
What are you waiting for?

39
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,597
But he...

40
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,092
he saved our lives when we were starving.

41
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:18,660
He gave us food.

42
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:28,157
Okay, I don't see why you're all so upset.

43
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,800
I Didn't sink it

44
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:33,000
Back off sure boy.

45
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:39,660
It's not your fight, but I
will what I'm going to sink it

46
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:47,495
You bastard, that's what you're doing.

47
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:49,357
You can't sink this shit,

48
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:52,957
but if the restaurant's gone There's
no reason to attack then, is there?

49
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:53,870
No!

50
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,500
This ship saved my life.

51
00:02:57,960 --> 00:03:01,780
I owe everything to her, and
you will not take that away!

52
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:04,729
You're gonna die for
a dumb old restaurant?

53
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,120
Are you stupid?

54
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:07,440
What'd you say?

55
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:09,060
Getting killed?

56
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,294
That's how you want to repay your debt?

57
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:16,289
The old man didn't save you so
that you could kill yourself.

58
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,897
He did it so you could do
something with your life.

59
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:21,140
Not to die like a fool!

60
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:24,240
And so your big idea is
to help them attack us?

61
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,869
Boys, there's no need
for friends to fight,

62
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:33,078
especially when there's
nothing either of you can do.

63
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,437
Not while there's a big shotgun

64
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:38,461
pressed right up against
the old man's chef's hat.

65
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:42,874
Your problem began when you decided
to come up against the Krieg pirates.

66
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,520
Fire, Pearl!

67
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:47,280
Now you will burn!

68
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:01,990
Ginny!

69
00:04:02,073 --> 00:04:04,440
What did you do?

70
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,910
Ginny?

71
00:04:05,993 --> 00:04:07,020
I'm sorry, Pearl.

72
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,160
You're in my way.

73
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,310
Ginny!

74
00:04:14,393 --> 00:04:16,867
You have betrayed your
captain and your ship!

75
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,157
I'm sorry, Dunkrie.

76
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,593
But he saved our lives.

77
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:20,817
I can't kill him.

78
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:21,730
Not like this.

79
00:04:21,813 --> 00:04:22,860
He deserves better.

80
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,940
He deserves to face death standing up.

81
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:31,440
But I promise you, he'll
still die by my hand.

82
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:37,997
Oh, great.

83
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:41,800
My chief commander has now
completely lost his marbles.

84
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:44,400
He's their chief commander?

85
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,080
I guess.

86
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,157
Did you see him crush that guy, though?

87
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:50,580
One blow and his shield was in pieces.

88
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:51,880
Now that's power.

89
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,600
My plan worked perfectly.

90
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:59,117
And now he's out in the open.

91
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,030
You liar.

92
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:03,061
There's no way you thought
that this would happen.

93
00:05:04,020 --> 00:05:04,850
Sanji.

94
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:08,997
Look, I don't want to ruin this ship,
but I think it's too late for that.

95
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,817
You're going to get to this
restaurant without killing me?

96
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,417
You got another thing coming.

97
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:14,380
Sounds fair.

98
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:17,464
And it will be an absolute
pleasure to kill you.

99
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,100
My good friend.

100
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,640
Gee, that's comforting.

101
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:23,370
Asshole.

102
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,200
You as well, chore boy.

103
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:30,120
Gee, thanks, but I'm not
afraid of any Krieg pirate.

104
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:34,100
Little dwarf!

105
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:36,813
I'm right here ready to die, little man.

106
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,577
I'm gonna stuff that stupid
Straw Hat right down your throat.

107
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:43,580
We're the three pirates,
rulers of the East Blue.

108
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:49,659
Hmm, only because you outnumbered
the other pirates in the East Blue.

109
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:59,860
Oh boy, now you really pissed
him off. Guess I was right.

110
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,140
You're dead meat!

111
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:02,480
Let's get him!

112
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,160
Hold your place!

113
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:08,480
But Don Krieg, he can't say that!

114
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:13,192
You only prove his point when you lose
control or whine like little babies.

115
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,600
You see me trembling with anger?

116
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:19,240
Only the weak react to mere words.

117
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,600
Donkreek pirates run from no man!

118
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,320
Yes, sir!

119
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:29,140
Gain, it's your job to
take care of that cook.

120
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,720
I'll handle the little boy.

121
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,860
That brat is all mine.

122
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:37,457
I understand.

123
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,700
Yes, Donkreek.

124
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,760
Hey, boy,

125
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:46,720
you can try your devil
fruit magic against me,

126
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:51,253
but I've seen it all before and have
never been defeated by such trickery.

127
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:55,720
When you experience the full force
that conquered the entire East Blue,

128
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:59,260
then you'll understand the
meaning of power, chore boy.

129
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:01,679
Your voice is getting on my nerves.

130
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,252
I'm gonna kick your ass.

131
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:04,693
It's as simple as that.

132
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:07,460
Hold on just a second.

133
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:09,160
I'll be right there.

134
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,240
The impudence.

135
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:19,600
That cook is done for now. Yeah, man.

136
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:23,057
When Ginny takes out his weapons,
he's through-screwing around.

137
00:07:23,140 --> 00:07:24,180
Just look at him.

138
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:31,900
They call him a cold-hearted demon.

139
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:37,080
He's our cool-headed, cold-hearted
Pirate Fleet Chief Commander, Ginny.

140
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:40,154
It doesn't matter if you beg for mercy,

141
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:43,261
he'll still laugh in your
face while he kills you.

142
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:49,140
I'm sorry, Sanji, but I can't be defeated.

143
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:51,717
Yeah, go ahead.

144
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:52,918
Tell yourself that.

145
00:07:58,580 --> 00:07:59,640
Here I come!

146
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:02,730
Ah!

147
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,780
Oh, yeah! You Sodom!

148
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:18,040
Ah-ha!

149
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:23,520
Ah! Ah!

150
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,080
Ah!

151
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:31,170
Ah!

152
00:08:31,253 --> 00:08:36,500
And now, it's time for
you to accept defeat.

153
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:54,780
Die!

154
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:22,700
That cook kicked Kaido in the head.

155
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:25,440
Yeah, I couldn't believe it.

156
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,357
Do you think he's still alive?

157
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:28,270
Enough!

158
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,670
Stop!

159
00:09:29,753 --> 00:09:33,804
After all this time, you should know a
hell of a lot better than that, you idiots.

160
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,906
There's a reason I trust him
above any of my other pirate crew.

161
00:09:38,380 --> 00:09:42,439
Ginny is always a cool-headed,
cold-hearted demon, and he never quits!

162
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:52,597
I can't believe Sanji is getting up.

163
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,092
He should lie back down.

164
00:09:54,380 --> 00:09:58,262
After what he's been through, his
ribs must be completely smashed.

165
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:05,860
Well, that wasn't too
bad, Chief Commander.

166
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:10,700
Let me know when you're
ready to really fight.

167
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:19,420
He's just sitting there.

168
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,480
Now it's ass-kicking time.

169
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:31,520
Don't hurt yourself.

170
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,680
You're a bastard!

171
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:50,577
Don't you want to fight me?

172
00:10:50,660 --> 00:10:51,640
Fight you?

173
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:53,320
Do I really have to?

174
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:56,756
If all I want to do is kill
you, that's enough for me.

175
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:03,697
Really don't have any patience
for your stupid games little fool.

176
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:07,760
Oh, yeah How about I butt your head off?

177
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,230
Sanchi!

178
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:25,637
Woo-hoo!

179
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,308
Pulverize the rest of them!

180
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,940
Yeah, what he said! Crap!

181
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:32,217
If only he hadn't fought
that pearl guy first!

182
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:36,065
Yeah, I don't think you'll survive
another hit from those balls.

183
00:11:37,860 --> 00:11:38,840
Go ahead.

184
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:41,220
You hit like a girl anyway.

185
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,140
He's too strong for me.

186
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:00,860
Now die.

187
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,340
Bye, Sanji.

188
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:09,340
What was that? Your pity?

189
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:13,360
I'm not dead yet!

190
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,360
Chief Commander!

191
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:20,460
Oh no!

192
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:25,570
No!

193
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:26,720
He can't take it!

194
00:12:26,860 --> 00:12:29,507
He's gonna kill himself
just trying to fight!

195
00:12:53,860 --> 00:12:56,040
Damn bastard.

196
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:23,900
I can't, Dahlkrieg!

197
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:25,900
I won't do it!

198
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:31,900
I can't!

199
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,000
I'm sorry, Captain.

200
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,940
What did you say?

201
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:43,820
I won't do what you want.

202
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:45,768
Take it and leave me alone.

203
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,220
I'm sorry.

204
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:54,820
I'm sorry.

205
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,239
Thank you so much.

206
00:13:56,380 --> 00:13:57,740
I thought it was over.

207
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,019
I truly thought I was going to die.

208
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:07,220
This food, it's delicious.

209
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:10,120
I've never eaten food this could before.

210
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:11,760
Of course it is.

211
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:19,950
Sorry.

212
00:14:20,033 --> 00:14:24,077
You'll probably get yelled at or fired
because you gave me that food for free.

213
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:27,984
Now there's not proof, so there's
no way for me to get yelled at.

214
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:36,360
He treated me with such respect
and decency and kindness.

215
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:43,140
That's why I can't bring
myself to kill him.

216
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:45,460
Don't get caught again.

217
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,740
I've always been loyal to you.

218
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:53,106
Up till now, I've believed
in what we've done.

219
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:56,520
I respect you and appreciate
all you have given me.

220
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,620
Trusting me as your chief
commander was the honor of my life.

221
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,040
Until this moment,

222
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:08,537
I have obeyed every single order you have
given me without ever questioning it.

223
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:13,800
I can't live with myself if I kill
this man, and I cannot break my oath.

224
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:21,160
Please, I beg you, let me
disobey just this one order.

225
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:25,760
Please, Don Krieg.

226
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:31,380
Listen, can't we just leave?

227
00:15:31,560 --> 00:15:34,148
They can keep the
restaurant for themselves.

228
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:38,320
You little son of a bitch!

229
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:42,200
You think you can defy my orders
and then tell me what to do?

230
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:45,917
It's pathetic.

231
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:50,920
Morality, sympathy, weaknesses I
never expected to see from you.

232
00:15:51,460 --> 00:15:53,840
You are not my chief commander anymore!

233
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,017
Pirates step aside.

234
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:06,637
No, not the gas.

235
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:08,697
He's going to use the MH5.

236
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:10,560
We're all gonna die.

237
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,577
What? Who's in gas?

238
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:14,937
Where's my mask?

239
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:17,720
Masks on. Move it. Move it.

240
00:16:17,860 --> 00:16:19,037
He's using MH5.

241
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,497
Gas is a coward's weapon.

242
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:21,410
You bastard.

243
00:16:21,493 --> 00:16:22,338
You'll kill us all.

244
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:25,240
The only thing that matters in a battle

245
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:29,957
is who ends up winning, even
if more have got to die.

246
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:32,120
Poison gas is just a means to

247
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:34,930
an end.

248
00:16:35,013 --> 00:16:37,897
Victory is all that decides
what's right and what's wrong.

249
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,180
If you are dead,

250
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,837
nobody's gonna hear you complain anyway.

251
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:47,260
When you don't hesitate to do
unspeakable, horrible things,

252
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:51,140
that is true power.

253
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:55,530
He's insane.

254
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,394
Might as well throw that gas mask away!

255
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:09,500
You're no longer worthy
to be a Karoo pirate.

256
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:11,610
Die!

257
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:22,240
I'm not going to let
that happen, you bastard!

258
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:24,391
You're wasting your time!

259
00:17:24,940 --> 00:17:25,770
Tribute!

260
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:39,810
Crap!

261
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,110
Keen!

262
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:49,140
You don't have to listen to that blowhard,
because I'm going to kick his ass!

263
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:50,770
No!

264
00:17:50,860 --> 00:17:52,625
My captain cannot be defeated!

265
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:57,920
Don Krieg is the strongest man
alive, and I respect his punishment.

266
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,360
Will you please snap out of it?

267
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:02,480
He is going to kill you!

268
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,620
I deserve it.

269
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:08,285
Obeying my emotions meant
betraying my captain.

270
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:11,977
If I were in his position, then
I would have done the same thing.

271
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:15,080
And now, death is the
only honor I have left.

272
00:18:17,420 --> 00:18:18,250
George!

273
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:19,970
Why?

274
00:18:21,420 --> 00:18:23,940
Heh, so you've remembered your place.

275
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:26,440
But it's much too late for that.

276
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:28,940
Now you will both die together.

277
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,060
It's the MH5!

278
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:34,460
Poison, gas bomb, fire!

279
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:44,360
Get inside the restaurant!

280
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:49,380
Thank you!

281
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:51,840
Sanji King! Catch!

282
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:54,760
Now for mine!

283
00:18:55,620 --> 00:18:57,020
Where'd they go?

284
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:17,580
This is power!

285
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:35,800
I'm alive!

286
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:38,022
That mask appeared just in time!

287
00:19:44,140 --> 00:19:45,940
What a crazy bastard.

288
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:47,780
He tried to kill us all.

289
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,628
That guy's gotta be insane.

290
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,957
I can't believe he used poison gas.

291
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,260
He must be a demon.

292
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,833
No human would do that.

293
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:11,600
Do you think Sanji and Shura
Boy made it? I don't know.

294
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:14,760
Look, the poison gas is clearing up.

295
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:25,610
Ginny!

296
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:30,400
Let go!

297
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:32,920
You can let go now!

298
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,960
Hey Ginny, are you okay?

299
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:44,040
It's your mask you gave it to me.

300
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:53,240
What a fool you are paying for a
plate of food with your life oh!

301
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:58,100
Well maybe you'll learn when you're dead.

302
00:21:08,860 --> 00:21:09,690
Ginny.

303
00:21:14,760 --> 00:21:17,440
So, it seems...

304
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:23,620
Don Krieg was not the right
man for you to follow, was he?

305
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:32,880
It figures that you still feel for
that pathetic scum. Scum? That's right!

306
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:37,100
Anyone who loses focus and betrays
my ship is worthless to me.

307
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:39,556
They'll almost certainly do it again.

308
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:42,477
Putting him out of his misery
is an act of mercy to keep him

309
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:46,266
from dishonoring himself in the
future and endangering my crew.

310
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,857
But he just...

311
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:51,157
I never thought the captain
would kill his chief commander.

312
00:21:51,240 --> 00:21:52,070
I know.

313
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:56,017
Ginny has been his right-hand man for even
longer than I've been part of the crew.

314
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:56,930
That's right.

315
00:21:57,013 --> 00:22:01,645
See, no one's ever showed more loyalty to
Don Krieg than Ginny has over the years.

316
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:04,997
How could he forget what Ginny
did for us after we escaped

317
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:07,957
from the Grand Line and
full-body's marines were after us?

318
00:22:08,040 --> 00:22:09,677
It was a miracle we escaped.

319
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:13,980
Yeah, he was willing to sacrifice
his life for us by acting as a decoy.

320
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:17,057
Without him, we wouldn't
have made it out of there.

321
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:20,457
Gein's laid down his life for
Don Krieg a hundred times easy.

322
00:22:20,540 --> 00:22:24,364
I can't believe the captain would
kill him with such little care.

323
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,160
That's so cruel.

324
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,420
Patty, get the kit, hurry!

325
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:32,500
It's for food poisoning.

326
00:22:32,820 --> 00:22:34,977
I don't think it'll work on gas, Sanji.

327
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:35,890
I don't care.

328
00:22:35,973 --> 00:22:36,803
We have to try.

329
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,077
Put the mask on him.

330
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:40,600
It will detoxify the gas in his lungs.

331
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:42,997
Then bring him upstairs
and let him breathe.

332
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:45,492
It's the only chance we have to save him.

333
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,100
Patty, Carney, hurry. Help me.

334
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:55,380
All right already. Me too.

335
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:56,954
All right, I'm coming.

336
00:22:58,060 --> 00:22:59,117
It's no use.

337
00:22:59,200 --> 00:23:01,760
He's going to die within the hour.

338
00:23:04,420 --> 00:23:06,580
Don't you dare die, Ginny!

339
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:11,000
You can't let someone like him win!

340
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:14,177
Stick around, now I'm mad!

341
00:23:14,260 --> 00:23:17,319
You'll want to see what I'm
going to do to him next!

342
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:21,280
You can't defeat him!

343
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:25,597
Wait a second, attacking him
head on is exactly what he wants!

344
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,120
He's strongest that way!

345
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:31,340
I'm not worried!

346
00:23:32,340 --> 00:23:34,857
Go ahead and give it your best shot!

347
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:36,257
Dumb kid!

348
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:39,500
When you lose your patience,
you become easy prey!

349
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:43,757
You are only running toward
one thing, chore boy!

350
00:23:43,840 --> 00:23:45,157
And that is!

351
00:23:45,240 --> 00:23:47,257
He's dead, really dead!

352
00:23:47,340 --> 00:23:48,697
Your funeral!

353
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:50,000
My funeral?

354
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:56,470
Oh, no!

355
00:23:56,553 --> 00:23:57,417
Get out of there!

356
00:23:57,500 --> 00:24:01,480
He got hit.

357
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:07,537
He's done!

358
00:24:07,620 --> 00:24:09,800
Poor guy.

359
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:20,830
Here we go!

360
00:24:20,913 --> 00:24:21,743
Just try it!

361
00:24:22,200 --> 00:24:23,671
He's got no place to hit!

362
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:27,390
Castle!

363
00:24:30,700 --> 00:24:31,530
No!

364
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:48,320
Don Krieg is down!

365
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:49,640
That punk got him!

366
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:51,471
What is that kid, anyway?

367
00:24:51,940 --> 00:24:54,580
He punched him right through the spanks!

368
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:00,320
That's messed up.

369
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:04,020
I've never seen him get hit
in any kind of fight, ever.

370
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:09,977
He busted right through that porcupine
cape and smashed him right in the face.

371
00:25:10,060 --> 00:25:12,000
I, I can't believe it.

372
00:25:19,400 --> 00:25:21,460
So is this my funeral?

373
00:25:22,540 --> 00:25:23,370
Yours!

374
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:26,700
You can't kill me.

375
00:25:27,580 --> 00:25:28,960
Little spikes.

376
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:31,980
My funeral.

377
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:36,820
Will take more than this!

378
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:41,580
You'll have to do better than that?

379
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:44,980
if you want to beat me.

380
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:51,535
Because I don't think it's
time for me to die just yet.

381
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:11,360
I know one thing. He's nuts.

382
00:26:15,900 --> 00:26:18,157
I've seen one or two like him before.

383
00:26:18,240 --> 00:26:21,517
Stubborn kids who'd rather die than have

384
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:23,677
to turn away from a
fight once it's started.

385
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:27,877
He'll stay that's for sure.

386
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:32,437
I'm glad he's with us because
guys like that are hell to fight.

387
00:26:32,520 --> 00:26:38,077
I don't care if he wins or loses.

388
00:26:38,160 --> 00:26:41,477
I consider it an honor just to be able?

389
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:43,089
I'll be able to watch him.

390
00:27:11,560 --> 00:27:13,957
Was in my grasp.

391
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:16,620
And I wouldn't let go.

392
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:21,897
My only dream.

393
00:27:21,980 --> 00:27:27,397
I won't stop chasing it.

394
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:29,860
Until it comes true.

395
00:27:31,300 --> 00:27:35,177
But if the world ever changes!

396
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:38,397
I call out your name.

397
00:27:38,480 --> 00:27:44,980
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

398
00:27:45,660 --> 00:27:51,960
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

399
00:27:52,740 --> 00:27:57,320
Waiting for that one true dream?
